small CSS tip for icons:

you can use an SVG as a mask instead of putting it directly in your markup.

.𝚒𝚌𝚘𝚗 {
  𝚠𝚒𝚍𝚝𝚑: 𝟸𝟶𝚙𝚡;
  𝚑𝚎𝚒𝚐𝚑𝚝: 𝟸𝟶𝚙𝚡;

  𝚖𝚊𝚜𝚔: 𝚞𝚛𝚕("/𝚒𝚌𝚘𝚗𝚜/𝚌𝚑𝚎𝚌𝚔.𝚜𝚟𝚐") 𝚌𝚎𝚗𝚝𝚎𝚛 / 𝚌𝚘𝚗𝚝𝚊𝚒𝚗 𝚗𝚘-𝚛𝚎𝚙𝚎𝚊𝚝;
  𝚋𝚊𝚌𝚔𝚐𝚛𝚘𝚞𝚗𝚍: 𝚌𝚞𝚛𝚛𝚎𝚗𝚝𝙲𝚘𝚕𝚘𝚛;
}

the SVG only defines the shape.
CSS controls the color, size and states.

pretty useful for icon systems where the same icon appears across different themes and components.

